        "description": "<div>The SRPC Tax Parcel Viewer displays parcel data for all 18 municipalities in the Strafford region. The viewer also displays a variety of other data such as soil types, floodplains, steep slopes, wetlands, aquifers, impervious coverage, and others. This map viewer provides baseline data for a variety of local and regional planning efforts, and is used frequently by municipal planners, regional planners, conservation commissions, planning boards, and others. The parcel viewer provides detailed parcel assessing data for many of our communities. Assessing data can be viewed by clicking on a parcel and reading the associated pop-up window.</div><div><br /></div>The SRPC Tax Parcel Viewer was created in 2020 and is regularly updated to the best of our ability.",
        "licenseInfo": "<span style='font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:13.3333px;'>Data should be used for planning purposes only.</span><span style='font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:13.3333px;'>  </span><span style='font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:13.3333px;'>Data were derived from various sources and were updated at different timeframes, with varying levels of accuracy, and therefore errors are often inherent in GIS data.</span><span style='font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:13.3333px;'>  </span><span style='font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:13.3333px;'>In most cases, the presented data is only a subset of the original data.</span><span style='font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:13.3333px;'>  </span><span style='font-family:&quot;Century Gothic&quot;, sans-serif; font-size:13.3333px;'>Please visit the original location of the data, contact the original host source for the data, or contact SRPC for a copy of the full data set.</span>",
